      "review_notes": "Canonical binomial thinning and filling identify the two binary-refinement branches. The expected unresolved population is n/2, funding fixed3/2 error amplification with potential n\u03b4. The CTE proof draws one supported fair-binomial split, follows either branch and applies the same induction hypothesis; \u03b5/(n+1) removes the auxiliary potential. Independent tests check exact nondyadic bias1/3, one-trial atom1/3, mean1 for three1/3 trials, zero-trial and zero/full-bias Dirac laws, the complete two-fair-trial arbitrary-ENNReal expectation, infinite credits and generic framing."
    },
