      "review_notes": "The deterministic table replicates each label exactly its weight. A table lookup theorem identifies a uniform position with the existing categorical rank partition; its canonical normalized law is WeightedChoice.law. A short raw syntax helper inserts only a locally closed tail continuation, keeping binder capture bookkeeping outside the main proof. The program logic transparently validates, expands, sums, draws a uniform rank and looks up the table. Tests check [0,2,0] and [1,0,2] tables, the unique positive label, infinite credit at zero-weight labels and generic framing."
    },
