      "review_notes": "Multiply-high reduction accepts exactly those source words whose low product is at least the Euclidean remainder. The accepted fibre for each label is an explicit interval of length floor(width/n), so finite fibrewise summation proves the exact uniform law. The remaining short mass pays doubled retry credit. Tests compute the n5/width8 accepted set {1,3,4,6,7}, show its quotient image is all five labels, check the boundary low product at source7, the complete arbitrary-ENNReal kernel, zero-bit singleton and framed clients."
